Thanks again for this example code. I got it working yesterday and at this point I have one main question. The code sets up a function (run_um) to run unmarked in each core which I've adapted to include 15 arguments (i.e., 16 cores minus one) and then uses parLapply() to run the function on a list of lists (called args) containing unmarked calls. That is all very straightforward and works just fine, but could require quite a bit of re-coding for each model run to ensure the number of desired models is handled by the number of available cores (e.g., in this case we could fit 15 models, then would have to set it up with another "args" list for the next run of 15 models). I'm wondering if a more flexible approach exists that would let the code cycle through available processors until all models are fit. Sort of like how you explained that parboot() now works (cycles N=1000 simulations through the available cores until they're all done). Do you how this approach could be used for fitting multiple models?

