Are you using the pre-release version of unmarked from Github? It has a new C++ backend for occuRN that should be faster (maybe up to 2x faster). Since Dan's function calls parboot and parboot repeatedly calls occuRN it should also speed things up for you.
If you decide to try this and re-run your test with nsim=10 I'd be curious to know if it speeds things up and if so how much.

devtools::install_github('rbchan/unmarked')

Also, you could consider just reducing the number of simulations you run.

